            <ArticleTitle>[Complications during directional coronary atherectomy (DCA): catheter fracture between housing assembly and shaft point with subsequent vascular occlusion].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>453-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Directional coronary atherectomy of a severe stenosis of the left anterior descending coronary artery was complicated by device fracture between the cylindric housing portion and the distal nose-cone collecting chamber. After successful removal of the DCA device, an early occlusion of the coronary vessel occurred, which could be successfully treated by perfusion balloon catheter.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
